{{!-- A PREP VIEW WITH NOTHING IN IT: a centred block in the pane — the view's own glyph in a washed
      circle, a heading, the sentence that says how things get here, a row of the kinds the view
      will take, and the button that starts one.

      WHY A BLOCK AND NOT A LINE. A new world opens every one of these views empty, and one grey
      sentence over a dashed bar in an otherwise empty window read as a pane that had failed to
      load. The glyph is the switcher segment's own (the same mask files, selected off `view` in
      stonetop.css), so the empty pane is recognisably the place the segment named.

      THE KINDS ROW IS A PROMISE THE DROP FILTER KEEPS. `accepts` is built in JS from the same
      table the drop zone and the card's pills read (gm-bundle-tab.js#acceptedKinds), so it cannot
      show a kind the pane refuses. Decoration for a sighted reader, `aria-hidden`: the sentence
      above it already says what to drag in, in words. Sites pass none, and the row is left out.

      THE BUTTON IS THE PANE BAR'S, moved here and made primary: the bar above an empty view is
      drawn `bare`. Same two classes, same handler hook, so it is the same act wherever it is
      pressed (gm-prep-pane-bar.hbs says why the hook has to stay inside the pane's scope).

      ONLY FOR A VIEW THAT HAS NEVER HAD ANYTHING. "You have run everything you prepared" is a
      different fact, and it keeps its own smaller line in the tab template: the advice there is
      to lift one back out of the fold, not to start from nothing.

      Hash parameters, rendered at the top of a pane and never inside an `{{#each}}` of the
      caller's, so they shadow nothing. Inside its own `{{#each accepts}}` every lookup is written
      `this.`, so the hash's `label` cannot answer for an item's. --}}
<div class="stonetop-gm-prep-empty stonetop-gm-prep-empty--{{this.view}}">
	<span class="stonetop-gm-prep-empty-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></span>
	<h3 class="stonetop-gm-prep-empty-title">{{this.title}}</h3>
	<p class="stonetop-gm-prep-empty-text">{{this.text}}</p>
	{{#if accepts.length}}
	<ul class="stonetop-gm-prep-empty-kinds" aria-hidden="true">
		{{#each accepts}}
		<li data-tooltip="{{this.label}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="{{this.icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i></li>
		{{/each}}
	</ul>
	{{/if}}
	<button type="button" class="stonetop-prep-add-btn stonetop-gm-pane-add stonetop-gm-pane-add--primary {{this.kind}}-add-btn"><i class="fas fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span class="stonetop-chip-text">{{this.label}}</span></button>
</div>
